# Motion: Full, then screen changes: the incoming screen slides in 12 px while the old one fades, and a click made during the
# fade reaches the new screen (it used to be swallowed): Versus, then the "No Knight" row 3 frames later.
# Settings layout: Settings (150,490); Display tab (880,172); Motion cycle (700,532); Back (125,25). Main menu Versus (150,250);
# "No Knight" row (905,344).
wait 20
click 150 490
wait 30
click 880 172
wait 20
click 700 532        # Motion: Reduced -> Full
wait 10
click 125 25         # Back: the main menu slides in from the left
wait 4
capture motion-screens-back-f4
wait 40
click 150 250        # Versus: forward, the mode list slides in from the right
wait 2
capture motion-screens-forward-f3
click 905 344        # a click during the fade: it picks "Simplify - No Knight"
wait 60
capture motion-screens-click-through
click 808 712        # Play: the game screen slides in as a whole (boards and HUD, not only the background)
wait 3
capture motion-screens-play-f3
